(Send signal 0 to process 999999. - a pid that does not exist - sets the
 error flag (ESRCH). signal 0 delivers nothing, so this is safe. On
 error then prints, proving the failure path mirrors the other syscall
 statements and that _last_error is set on a failed kill(2).)

Send signal 0 to process 999999.
On error print "no such process".